timestamp=2026-11-04T15:59:53.312Z level=INFO run=b196681e message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# TURB_OUTPUT_01 drops to exactly 770.0 which is below normal_min 800.0, so deviation starts at 17:00 observed. \n# Physical onset = 17:00 - 2 min = 16:58. That's very early.\n# Let us look at what happens just before - is it a sudden drop?\ndf1 = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/sensors_01.csv')\ndf2 = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/sensors_02.csv')\ndf3 = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/sensors_03.csv')\nmeta = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/sensor_metadata.csv')\nmeta = meta.set_index('sensor_id')\n\ndf1['timestamp'] = pd.to_datetime(df1['timestamp']).dt.tz_localize(None)\ndf2['timestamp'] = pd.to_datetime(df2['timestamp']).dt.tz_localize(None)\ndf3['timestamp'] = pd.to_datetime(df3['timestamp']).dt.tz_localize(None)\ndf = pd.concat([df1, df2, df3], ignore_index=True)\n\nsid = 'TURB_OUTPUT_01'\ng = df[df['sensor_id']==sid].sort_values('timestamp')\n# look around 16:55-17:05\nwindow = g[(g['timestamp'] >= pd.Timestamp('2024-01-15 16:55:00')) & \n           (g['timestamp'] <= pd.Timestamp('2024-01-15 17:05:00'))]\nprint(window.to_string(index=False))\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
