timestamp=2026-11-04T16:00:47.893Z level=INFO run=b196681e message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# So earliest physical onset is TURBINE at 16:58 (TURB_OUTPUT_01). \n# Then STEAM_GEN at 21:59 (STEAM_PRES_01). \n# Then COOLING at 00:09 (COOLING_PRES_01). \n# Then TURBINE other sensors (bear/vib/speed) at 00:59-01:01 - these are later physical onsets within TURBINE subsystem? They start deviating physically later than TURB_OUTPUT. That means different turbine sensors show physical deviation at different times. But we need the subsystem-level onset: \"the onset time of a subsystem is when its physical state first began to deviate from normal...\"\n# So each subsystem has one onset time - when that subsystem's physical state first began to deviate. That could be detected via any of its sensors. So we need the earliest (smallest time) first_phys_deviation among sensors of that subsystem.\ndf1 = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/sensors_01.csv')\ndf2 = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/sensors_02.csv')\ndf3 = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/sensors_03.csv')\nmeta = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/sensor_metadata.csv')\nmeta = meta.set_index('sensor_id')\n\ndf1['timestamp'] = pd.to_datetime(df1['timestamp']).dt.tz_localize(None)\ndf2['timestamp'] = pd.to_datetime(df2['timestamp']).dt.tz_localize(None)\ndf3['timestamp'] = pd.to_datetime(df3['timestamp']).dt.tz_localize(None)\ndf = pd.concat([df1, df2, df3], ignore_index=True)\ndf = df.sort_values(['sensor_id', 'timestamp']).reset_index(drop=True)\n\ndef is_deviating(row):\n    sid = row['sensor_id']\n    v = row['value']\n    m = meta.loc[sid]\n    return (v < m['normal_min']) or (v > m['normal_max'])\n\ndf['deviating'] = df.apply(is_deviating, axis=1)\nresults = []\nfor sid, g in df.groupby('sensor_id'):\n    g = g.sort_values('timestamp').copy()\n    devi_idx = g.index[g['deviating'] == True]\n    if len(devi_idx) == 0:\n        continue\n    first_obs = g.loc[devi_idx[0], 'timestamp']\n    m = meta.loc[sid]\n    delay = pd.Timedelta(minutes=float(m['response_delay_minutes']))\n    first_phys = first_obs - delay\n    results.append({\n        'sensor_id': sid,\n        'subsystem': m['subsystem'],\n        'first_obs_deviation': first_obs,\n        'response_delay_min': m['response_delay_minutes'],\n        'first_phys_deviation': first_phys\n    })\nres = pd.DataFrame(results)\n# get earliest per subsystem\nsubsys_onset = res.groupby('subsystem')['first_phys_deviation'].min().sort_values()\nprint(subsys_onset.to_string())\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
