timestamp=2026-11-04T16:05:43.836Z level=INFO run=b196681e message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# STEAM_PRES jumps from ~65 to 71.5 at 20:00Z (observed), physical onset 19:59Z - shortly after turbine output dropped at 18:00Z. That fits: turbine trip causes steam pressure to rise rapidly (stop of steam flow to turbine), so steam generator pressure increases. This is a standard transient.\n# Then COOLING_PRES_01 first phys deviation at 00:09Z (next day). Let us look at it.\ndf1 = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/sensors_01.csv')\ndf2 = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/sensors_02.csv')\ndf3 = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/sensors_03.csv')\nmeta = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/sensor_metadata.csv')\nmeta = meta.set_index('sensor_id')\n\ndf1['timestamp'] = pd.to_datetime(df1['timestamp']).dt.tz_localize(None)\ndf2['timestamp'] = pd.to_datetime(df2['timestamp']).dt.tz_localize(None)\ndf3['timestamp'] = pd.to_datetime(df3['timestamp']).dt.tz_localize(None)\ndf = pd.concat([df1, df2, df3], ignore_index=True)\ndf['offset_h'] = df['sensor_id'].map(lambda s: meta.loc[s, 'logger_utc_offset_hours'])\ndf['timestamp_utc'] = df['timestamp'] - pd.to_timedelta(df['offset_h'], unit='h')\n\ncp = df[df['sensor_id']=='COOLING_PRES_01'].sort_values('timestamp_utc')\nprint(cp[(cp['timestamp_utc'] >= pd.Timestamp('2024-01-15 23:55:00')) & \n         (cp['timestamp_utc'] <= pd.Timestamp('2024-01-16 00:20:00'))].to_string(index=False))\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
