timestamp=2026-11-04T16:06:59.101Z level=INFO run=b196681e message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# Let us also check STEAM_GEN other sensors' onset times more carefully. STEAM_PRES_01 is at 19:59Z; others like STEAM_DELTA_01, FEED_01, TEMP_01 have much later physical onsets (05:10Z+). That suggests the pressure was the first to be affected in steam generator - consistent with pressure rise due to turbine trip (steam can't flow out). That fits the physical cascade.\n# Similarly for COOLING, only COOLING_PRES_01 deviates early (00:09Z); temperature/flow/delta-T deviate later (02:21Z+). That indicates a pressure-related disturbance in cooling system occurring after the steam generator pressure changed. Or perhaps related to condenser cooling response to turbine trip.\n# This all points to the cascade starting at TURBINE, propagating to STEAM_GEN (pressure surge), then to COOLING, then affecting PRIMARY_LOOP, and finally CORE. So the order is TURBINE, STEAM_GEN, COOLING, PRIMARY_LOOP, CORE.\n# Let us write the answer accordingly.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
